{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "scale-county-timeagg-year-toxics-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.69, step 7f. `scale-county-timeagg-year-toxics`: `scale-county-timeagg-year`'s months (January, April, July and October 2020), day types, hours and road types with `<aggregateBy key=\"Year\"/>` and `<outputtimestep value=\"Year\"/>`, over the same county database (`inputs/washtenaw-county-timeagg.esm`), for the gasoline passenger car (21) and the diesel combination long-haul truck (62), selecting at RUNNING EXHAUST everything `scale-county-timeagg-year` does not check there but particulate matter -- CH4, N2O, NH3, SO2, NO, NO2, HONO, NMHC, NMOG, TOG, VOC, NonHAPTOG, the fifteen gaseous air toxics, Total Energy, Atmospheric CO2 and CO2 Equivalent, beside THC, CO and NOx -- and the same at START EXHAUST but N2O, CO2 Equivalent and the six ATRatio toxics (benzene, ethanol, 1,3-butadiene, formaldehyde, acetaldehyde, acrolein), which the model does not compute at start at any aggregation (PLAN.md §7.3.69). MOVESOutput is 27,782 rows; NonHAPTOG has none (see `db_movesoutput`).\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES is every species calculator over PreAggYEAR.sql's month collapse: ATRatio, which PreAggYEAR.sql would average per month group but which is EMPTY when it runs -- FuelEffectsGenerator writes it afterwards, at the one month group 0, from the collapsed formulations and the MonthGroupWeighting mean of ATBaseEmissions (FuelEffectsGenerator.java:1522-1975) -- ATRatioNonGas, minorHAPRatio and pahGasRatio, keyed by no month; methaneTHCRatio, hcSpeciation and nono2ratio through the supplied fuel subtype; SO2 through the supplied sulfur; and CO2 Equivalent over three parents. Every one is a share-weighted mean over the collapsed FuelSupply, whose shares sum to 0.334 of the year (F63). It found two things the month collapse changes (PLAN.md §7.3.69): AirToxicsCalculator multiplies VOC by the RAW FuelSupply share per formulation, so every toxic carries the fuel type's total twice (finding F70); and PreAggYEAR.sql's FuelSupply holds two E85 formulations, at which the altTHC quotient is a THC-weighted mean of each formulation's, not the exponential of the mean exponent (`cfr_suppliedAltQuotient`).\n\n`n_aggregatesMonths` is 1; `db_aggregationmonth` and `db_rateday` are read from its XML by `tools/runspec-month-selection.py` and `tools/runspec-day-selection.py`. `n_outputRate` is bound to 27782, the (pollutant-process, cohort) pairs of the one (county, month, day) cell; `n_physicsRow` 21, the two source types' physics rows.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "single-county-domain",
      "road-type-axis",
      "off-network-idle",
      "time-aggregation",
      "starts",
      "output-time-step",
      "year-aggregation",
      "air-toxics",
      "hc-speciation",
      "nox-speciation",
      "so2",
      "co2e"
    ]
  },
